**Exact Post-May 13, 2018 Audit Rule:** Under Note (1) and Note (2) to `§ 4.79` (`>= May 13, 2018`), **every clinic visit where an intravitreal/periocular injection, laser procedure, surgical intervention, or systemic immunosuppressant/biologic administration/adjustment is performed for treatment purposes counts as `1` qualifying treatment visit**:
• Every `8 weeks` (`6` injection visits/year) -> **`40%`** (`5–6` visits);
• Every `4 to 6 weeks` (`7–12` injection visits/year, or bilateral alternating-visit injections!) -> **`60%`** (`>= 7` visits)!

**Combining Visual Field Loss + Acuity Loss in the Same Eye (`§ 4.77(c)` & `DC 6080`):** Under **`38 C.F.R. § 4.77(c)`**, when **both** decreased visual acuity and a visual field defect are present in one or both eyes and are service-connected, VA must **separately evaluate** the visual acuity and the visual field defect (using `DC 6080`'s standalone percentage or its equivalent Snellen acuity `20/50` down to `5/200` on `DC 6065–6066`) **and combine them under `38 C.F.R. § 4.25`** (subject to `§ 4.75(d)`'s `30%` unilateral visual-impairment cap)!
• **Homonymous hemianopsia** *(loss of same right or left half of field in both eyes — classic post-TBI/stroke **`DC 6046` Post-chiasmal disorder** residual!)*: **`30%`**.
• **Loss of temporal half OR inferior half:** **`30%` bilateral** \| **`10%` unilateral** *(or evaluate affected eye as **`20/70`**)*.
• **Loss of nasal half OR superior half:** **`10%` bilateral** \| **`10%` unilateral** *(or evaluate affected eye as **`20/50`**)*.
• **Concentric Contraction (`Remaining Average Field Radius`):**
• **`<= 5°`:** **`100%` bilateral (+ `SMC(l)` under `§ 3.350(b)(2)`!)** \| **`30%` unilateral** *(or evaluate as **`5/200`**)*;
• **`6° to 15°`:** **`70%` bilateral** \| **`20%` unilateral** *(or evaluate as **`20/200`**)*;
• **`16° to 30°`:** **`50%` bilateral** \| **`10%` unilateral** *(or evaluate as **`20/100`**)*;
• **`31° to 45°`:** **`30%` bilateral** \| **`10%` unilateral** *(or evaluate as **`20/70`**)*;
• **`46° to 60°`:** **`10%` bilateral** \| **`10%` unilateral** *(or evaluate as **`20/50`**)*.
• **`DC 6081` (Scotoma, unilateral):** Centrally located scotoma of any size, OR scotoma affecting at least one-quarter (`quadrantanopsia`) of the visual field -> **`10%`** *(combine or substitute acuity if higher)*.

**Goldmann `III/4e` Diplopia Mapping (`DC 6090`):** Mapped within `40°` of primary gaze (**Note:** occasional diplopia or diplopia **correctable with prism spectacles** is rated **`0%`** under `§ 4.31`):
• **Central `20 degrees`:** Equivalent to **`5/200`** (`30%` unilateral when paired with `20/40`);
• **`21° to 30°`:** **Down = `15/200`** (`20%`) \| **Lateral = `20/100`** (`10%`) \| **Up = `20/70`** (`10%`);
• **`31° to 40°`:** **Down = `20/200`** (`20%`) \| **Lateral = `20/70`** (`10%`) \| **Up = `20/40`** (`0%`).

**The `§ 4.78(b)(1)` One-to-Three Step Elevation Rule (CUE & Open-Claim Retroactive):**
• Assign an evaluation for diplopia to **ONLY ONE EYE** (never `DC 6090` bilaterally!).
• When the veteran has **BOTH diplopia AND decreased visual acuity or a visual field defect**, adjust the corrected visual acuity of the poorer eye (or the SC eye, if unilateral) poorer by:
• **`+1 step` poorer** if `DC 6090` diplopia equals **`20/70` or `20/100`**;
• **`+2 steps` poorer** if `DC 6090` diplopia equals **`20/200` or `15/200`**;
• **`+3 steps` poorer** if `DC 6090` diplopia equals **`5/200`** (capped at `5/200`, i.e., step-ups cannot fabricate `LPO`!).

**When PFTs Are Excused (`§ 4.96(d)(1)(i)–(iv)`):** PFTs are required to evaluate `DC 6600, 6603, 6604, 6825–6833, and 6840–6845` *except*:
• `(i)` When maximum exercise capacity test results are of record and are **`20 ml/kg/min` or less** (`< 15 ml/kg/min = 100%`; `15–20 ml/kg/min = 60%`);
• `(ii)` When **pulmonary hypertension** (documented by echocardiogram or cardiac catheterization), **cor pulmonale**, or **right ventricular hypertrophy** has been diagnosed (`= 100%`);
• `(iii)` When there have been one or more episodes of **acute respiratory failure** (`= 100%`); OR
• `(iv)` When **outpatient oxygen therapy** is required (`= 100%`). *(See also `§ 4.96(d)(3)` when an examiner states why PFTs are not a valid indication of respiratory functional impairment in a particular case).*

**The Three-Factor Compelling Circumstances Matrix (`38 C.F.R. § 3.12(e)(1)–(3)` — Applies ONLY to `(c)(6)` & `(d)(2)`):**
• **`(e)(1)` Length & Character of Service** exclusive of the period of prolonged AWOL or misconduct (honest, faithful, meritorious service, deployments, medals, promotions);
• **`(e)(2)(i)–(vii)` Reasons for Prolonged AWOL or Misconduct:**
• `(i)` **Mental or cognitive impairment** at the time of conduct—explicitly listing **PTSD, depression, bipolar disorder, schizophrenia, substance use disorder (`SUD`), ADHD, impulsive behavior, or cognitive disabilities** *(Crucial: a formal clinical diagnosis at the time of service is NOT required if lay/post-service evidence demonstrates impairment!)*;
• `(ii)` **Physical health**, including physical trauma and medication side effects;
• `(iii)` **Combat-related or overseas-related hardship**;
• `(iv)` **Sexual abuse / assault (`MST`)** or harassment;
• `(v)` **Duress, coercion, or desperation**;
• `(vi)` **Family obligations** or comparable obligations to third parties; and
• `(vii)` **Age, education, cultural background, and judgmental maturity**.
• **`(e)(3)` Valid Substantive UCMJ Legal Defense** that would have precluded conviction (going to guilt/innocence rather than technicalities).

**Qualifying Medical Pathways (`SAH` `§ 2101(a)` vs. `SHA` `§ 2101(b)`):**
• **Full `SAH` Grant (`38 U.S.C. § 2101(a)(2)(B)`; `38 C.F.R. § 3.809` — CPI-indexed past `~$117,000+` in FY 2024–2026):** Permanent and total SC (or `§ 1151`) disability due to:
• Loss or loss of use (`LOU`) of **both lower extremities** precluding locomotion without braces, crutches, canes, or a wheelchair;
• **Blindness in both eyes having central visual acuity of `20/200` or less** in the better eye with corrective lenses (**expanded by `Pub. L. 116-154`, eff. Oct. 1, 2020**—eliminating the harsh pre-Oct. 1, 2020 rule that required *either* light-perception-only/5-degree concentric contraction *or* blindness plus a missing leg!);
• Loss or `LOU` of **one lower extremity** together with `(a)` **residuals of organic disease or injury** affecting balance or propulsion so as to preclude locomotion without braces/crutches/canes/wheelchair, OR `(b)` loss/`LOU` of **one upper extremity** affecting balance/propulsion;
• Loss or `LOU` of **one lower extremity** occurring after Sept. 11, 2001 making it medically infeasible to ambulate without a wheelchair (capped at **`120` grants per fiscal year** post-Oct. 1, 2020 under `Pub. L. 116-154`, up from `30`);
• **Severe burn injuries** (full-thickness or deep partial-thickness burns with scar contractures); OR
• **Amyotrophic Lateral Sclerosis (`ALS`)** (`38 C.F.R. § 3.809(d)` — **automatic `SAH` eligibility** upon service connection under `38 C.F.R. § 3.318` without waiting for end-stage paralysis; see [Playbook 07](/playbooks/07-statutory-presumptions-chronic-tropical-pow-als)!).
• **`SHA` Grant (`38 U.S.C. § 2101(b)`; `38 C.F.R. § 3.809a` — CPI-indexed `~$23,000+`):** Anatomical loss or `LOU` of **both hands**, certain severe respiratory injuries (`Pub. L. 116-154`), or qualifying deep partial-thickness burns not meeting `SAH`.
• **`TRA` Grant (`38 U.S.C. § 2102A`):** Temporary adaptation grant (`~$47,000+` `SAH` / `~$8,400+` `SHA`) when the veteran resides **temporarily** in a home owned by a **family member**—and under `38 U.S.C. § 2102A(c)`, `TRA` funds **do NOT reduce** the veteran's aggregate lifetime `SAH`/`SHA` grant pool!

**Automatic SC Traumatic Brain Injury (`TBI`) -> Five Secondary Illnesses (`38 C.F.R. § 3.310(d)`):**
• Enacted at **`78 FR 76196` (pub. Dec. 17, 2013, eff. Jan. 16, 2014)**: Absent clear evidence to the contrary, five diagnosable illnesses are **presumed secondary to an in-service SC TBI (`DC 8045`)** based on initial TBI severity (`§ 3.310(d)(3)` stratification table: imaging, `LOC`, `AOC`, `PTA`, `GCS`):
• **Parkinsonism** (including Parkinson's disease, `DC 8004`) following **moderate or severe** TBI *(no time limit)*;
• **Unprovoked seizures** (`DC 8910–8914`) following **moderate or severe** TBI *(no time limit)*;
• **Certain dementias** (presenile Alzheimer-type, frontotemporal, and Lewy body dementia) manifesting within **15 years** of **moderate or severe** TBI;
• **Depression** (`DC 9434`) manifesting within **3 years** of **moderate or severe** TBI, **OR within 12 months of mild TBI**; and
• **Diseases of hormone deficiency** resulting from hypothalamo-pituitary changes manifesting within **12 months** of **moderate or severe** TBI.
• *Fallback Mandate (`§ 3.310(d)(2)`):* Even if a veteran had a **mild** TBI or manifested outside the `12-month / 3-year / 15-year` window (e.g., Parkinsonism or seizures after blast-related mild TBI), VA **must still adjudicate standard secondary nexus under `§ 3.310(a)`-(b)**!

**High-Value VHA / VistA Discovery Targets (Request via FOIA/Privacy Act Beyond Standard `CAPRI`):**
• **`iMedConsent` Electronic Informed-Consent Packets (`38 C.F.R. § 17.32`)** (verify signature, witness, procedure scope, and disclosed risks);
• **VHA Institutional Disclosure of Adverse Event** notes (VHA policy mandates formal disclosure to the veteran/family when VA care causes serious injury/death);
• **Radiology "View Alert" / Unread Imaging Logs**, **Pathology Addendum Timestamps**, **Medication Administration Records (`BCMA`)**, and **VAMC Police / Patient Safety Incident Reports** (crucial for *Viegas* equipment/facility defects!).
